usage: rot [-h] [--version]
           {check,replay,ci,demo,report,corpus,license,trace,coach,runtime,site,doctor,ladder,ab}
           ...

ROTN -- temporal policy verification engine (sound core, zero dependencies).

positional arguments:
  {check,replay,ci,demo,report,corpus,license,trace,coach,runtime,site,doctor,ladder,ab}
    check               verify a policy; emit verdict + attack.jsonl
    replay              re-derive a recorded attack.jsonl
    ci                  CI gate: verdict + JUnit XML + SARIF
    demo                the beachhead demo: rule -> attack -> proof -> coach
                        -> attestation (one command)
    report              the one-pager as an ATTESTATION (B3): --one-pager
                        --trace FILE emits Markdown + HTML; --verify-trace
                        FILE --expect HASH re-derives the trace hash (the re-
                        verify step)
    corpus              run the AWS Dogwood corpus
    license             manage Caravel licenses (Phase D): verify / make /
                        show
    trace               emit the RTF v1 deterministic, hashable reasoning
                        trace
    coach               coach the agent back in bounds, *with a proof* (the
                        CoachingArtifact: corrected policy + rationale + re-
                        proof)
    runtime             the runtime plane (Product 2): enforce rules on live
                        tool calls (eval / serve)
    site                regenerate the replay site's RTF trace data + registry
                        (the Ship plane: a pure function of the sample
                        policies)
    doctor              diagnose the ROTN installation (Python, package,
                        engines; --deep runs a real self-test)
    ladder              ==SUPPRESS==
    ab                  ==SUPPRESS==

optional arguments:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --version             show program's version number and exit
